{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers","id":1492812,"title":"Starting a Space Opera Game (looking for friendly kibitzers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-11T10:28:35-07:00","id":1492812,"title":"Starting a Space Opera Game (looking for friendly kibitzers)","content":"What it says on the tin. I hope to start a Space Opera Campaign more or less using M:tA. PCs will start as the equivalent of Star Trek ensigns. I'll use the standard starting template for Mages, with a few required skills (they are space explorers). Beefing up the Consors template will be necessary. <br /> <br /> I'm adding spheres. The Spheres of Society and Information are decided on. I'll describe them later. I need a twelfth sphere. <br /> <br /> All Consors will have at least a few dots of Psionics. Telepathy to the ability to send and receive telepathic messages being required. <br /> <br /> I'll post details asking for suggestions and critiques.<br /> <br /> The setting will be in the future. Humanity had to flee the Earth the PCs will be part of the space fleet of a world founded by groups from the Council of the Traditions led by a powerful Hermetic. The world is terraformed and very &quot;Star Trek&quot; with plenty of &quot;Doctor Who&quot; touches. The main rival societies are a theocracy, a corporate state, and an oligarchy of another type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T11:38:21-07:00","id":1492816,"title":"","content":"In the corporate or oligarchic state, problems could be delegated to groups of adventurers. The ensigns could be sent on a spy mission, undercover as an adventuring group from the region. First, they would have to observe locals and learn to speak and jest as they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T11:45:09-07:00","id":1492817,"title":"","content":"I've decided Changelings will be an allowed type too. Mages, Changelings, and psis make an acceptable group. The crossover issues of adding Garou, Fera, Cainites, Cathayans, Hunters, Mummies, Risen, or Wraiths, are simply too involved. <br /> <br /> I think I might need to add a Space Magic! Art to the Changeling magics. Space Magic! would cover telepathy, telempathy, telempathic projection, and similar territory.<br /> <br /> Councilor Troi, Nyssa of Traken, Maya from Space 1999, would all be best represented as Sidhe. Maya just has some really impressive shapeshifting skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-11-2022, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T12:55:59-07:00","id":1492822,"title":"","content":"I'd like to help with the Sphere thing; but first I need a better idea of what you have Society and Information doing.<br /> <br /> Some preliminary thoughts: MRev put forth the notion that the Spheres exist in triads, each corresponding to one of the three legs of the Metaphysical Trinity: Forces, Life, and Matter were the Pattern Spheres; Correspondence, Mind, and Time were the Dynamic Spheres; and Entropy, Prime, and Spirit were the Primordial Spheres. I could see revisiting this notion; but use four groups of three, and don't try to link them to a larger organizing principle \u2014 at least, not at first. <br /> <br /> \u2022 You have your Pattern Spheres: Forces, Life, and Matter. <br /> \u2022 Information, Mind, and Society strike me as a reasonable triad. <br /> \u2022 Correspondence and Time pair up nicely. <br /> \u2022 Prime and Entropy could also pair up.<br /> <br /> That leaves only Spirit. <br /> <br /> Would you be interested in splitting it in two? Make Dimensional Science something fundamentally distinct from Spirit, with the former focusing primarily on accessing other layers of reality (such as the Umbra) while Spirit focuses more exclusively on otherworldly entities. Put the former in with Correspondence and Time to define a trio that deals with overcoming separations (distance, time, and the Gauntlet, respectively), and put the latter in with Entropy and Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-11-2022, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:19:49-07:00","id":1492832,"title":"","content":"Spirit would go with Prime and Entropy. They already link those. The problem is something to link with Correspondence (Space) and Time. Space and Time keep everything from happening at once in the same place. I'd need to figure out what else does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:32:28-07:00","id":1492833,"title":"","content":"That's why I was suggesting splitting Dimensional Science off from Spirit: it can deal with access to other realms outside of conventional space. At its most basic level, it would let you sense connections to other worlds; at higher levels, it would let you manipulate the Gauntlet or its equivalent \u2014 whatever barrier stands between the two worlds. Conversely, Spirit <i>wouldn't</i> be able to do this; it would focus more heavily on interacting with spirits and spirit-stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:37:10-07:00","id":1492834,"title":"","content":"As I'm having three splats in the game Mages, Changelings, and Psis. I think each ages differently.<br /> <br /> Mages, their aging rate equals one divided by the Mages Arete. Thus an Arete 3 mage ages one third as fast as a normal human. <br /> <br /> Changelings, subtract their Banality from their Glamour. If this number is positive divide their aging rate by it. Thus a Glamour seven Banality five Changeling ages half as fast as a normal human. <br /> <br /> Psis ( and most healthy humans are Psis on this planet), take the square root of the total number of dots in psi powers, and numina counted as equal to psi for this purpose, round down to the nearest whole number and divide the Psi's aging rate by that. Thus a Psi with eight dots in psi powers and two more dots in numina counted as psi ages at one third the rate of a normal human.<br /> <br /> The few humans without Psi, Arete, or numina counted as Psi, have a lifespan of about one hundred ten years. After the age of twenty humans without Powers age about one year for every eighteen months on average. Humans on less advanced worlds age like humans in similar circumstances. There are worlds were aging is slower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:39:59-07:00","id":1492835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers?p=1492833#post1492833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I was suggesting splitting Dimensional Science off from Spirit: it can deal with access to other realms outside of conventional space. At its most basic level, it would let you sense connections to other worlds; at higher levels, it would let you manipulate the Gauntlet or its equivalent \u2014 whatever barrier stands between the two worlds. Conversely, Spirit <i>wouldn't</i> be able to do this; it would focus more heavily on interacting with spirits and spirit-stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mainly like that. Spirit should still let you go to the Spirit realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:45:31-07:00","id":1492836,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing the PCs as based on a world (tentative name Adocentyn, an Hermetic utopia from The Picatrix) settled by groups lead by Council Mages allied with Changelings. <br /> <br /> The world has a population like that of North America. <br /> <br /> The land sea ratio would be sixteen percent land eighty-four percent sea. But much more of that land would be arable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T15:51:16-07:00","id":1492843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers?p=1492832#post1492832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit would go with Prime and Entropy. They already link those. The problem is something to link with Correspondence (Space) and Time. Space and Time keep everything from happening at once in the same place. I'd need to figure out what else does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Causality, which is currently bundled into the Entropy Sphere.<br /> <br /> I toyed around with some possible metaphysical relationship diagrams for a twelve sphere model, but the overlap between some of the spheres makes it difficult. Mapping them to the fundamental properties of the universe to make them more sci-fi would need a massive overhaul.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed while playing around, consider changing a possible Society sphere into Emergence, which deals with emergent effects and should cover societal use (ie manipulating the outcome of interaction between entities).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T16:20:46-07:00","id":1492844,"title":"","content":"In my reworking of the Spheres for the Technocracy (where I use the term \u201cFields\u201d to distinguish them from the Spheres used by the Traditions), which removed the Sphere of Entropy entirely, I took the notion of causality and folded it into Time. I took the notion of decay and incorporate into the appropriate Pattern Spheres. And I took the notion of working with abstract patterns and folded it into Data.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to comment on Information or Society until I see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T20:26:13-07:00","id":1492855,"title":"","content":"As far as creating new worlds, I've found that Starfinder's Deck of Many Worlds is a useful tool for coming up with interesting and unique starting places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T16:54:49-07:00","id":1492937,"title":"","content":"The Council of Twelve differs from the C of 9 in these ways. The Verbena and the Dreamspeakers have merged (they have the seat of Spirit). This merger came about because they both got trashed in the crisis that forced the Mages off Earth. The technocratic union has collapsed. The Void Engineers hold the seat of Dimension. The Hermetics graciously allowed It X to take the seat of Force. The Hermetics now hold the Seat of Society/Community. The Progenitors have a new name and a vastly improved attitude and they hold the seat of Life. The Children of Knowledge hold the seat of Information. All other seats remain the same. <br /> <br /> The Dreamspeakers and the Verbena are working on bringing their insights to a modern world. They aren't wild about how things turned out but they'll deal. <br /> <br /> The Void Engineers are pleased with the set up and find the new Council congenital. <br /> <br /> It X is keeping it's collective heads down and working quietly towards its goals. But doesn't want to disrupt this group. <br /> <br /> The present fate of the NWO and the Syndicate are unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T14:53:46-07:00","id":1493025,"title":"","content":"Earth still exists in this setting. But humans and others need to leave it.<br /> <br /> The Methuselahs woke up, ancient creatures allied with the Oblivion broke through to the Fleshlands, vast wrym beasts roam freely, the Formians of all three courts plague the world.<br /> <br /> There are runs made to Earth. There are still harried bands of desperate survivors to be rescued.<br /> <br /> How do &quot;Others&quot; see these Mages?<br /> <br /> Vamps: If sane they want to escape too. The Mages avoid them like the plague. More powerful and less human vampires want to control a spaceship and crew for their own plans.<br /> <br /> Garou and Fera: Neither feel they can abandon Earth/Gaia. Both want breeding stock, and object to too many humans leaving Earth. Wyrm aligned shifters want to hunt on whatever world the space folk live on.<br /> <br /> Wraiths: Anchors and pathos already link many Wraiths to other worlds. Many of the Dark Kingdoms hunger to gain power in new realms. Others want to find safe places to heal.<br /> <br /> Mages: Many Mages not aligned with the Council still want to escape the Earth. Some of these would live in peace with the Council, others would always reject peace.<br /> <br /> Changelings: Most Changelings want to escape. The Thailian want to prevent all escape or go to the space folks world and make it a hell. The Leanhaun Sidhe are desperate to ruin or destroy the space folks worlds to finish the burden of their curse. Other Sidhe houses seek to rule/conquer the space folk.<br /> <br /> Hunters: They are divided. Most want to help rescue ordinary people and maybe escape as well. The Hermits and Waywards want to kill the Space Folk.<br /> <br /> Mummies: If tied to the Earth, they want to make people stay. If not tied, they want to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-31-2024, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T15:36:13-07:00","id":1493030,"title":"","content":"Another adventure path in this setting is Time Travel. The disrupted nature of this setting makes Time Travel possible, necessary, and dangerous. <br /> <br /> The PCs travelling back in time are seeking things like lost books, extinct animals, samples of various things. One traveler has shown a knack for getting samples of cheeses that allows the recreation of those cheeses. Seeds and cuttings of hundreds of useful plants have been brought to the future as well. <br /> <br /> Ships that sink with no known survivors give a possibility of rescuing people from the past. Maybe your PC was a Victorian Orphan being sent to distant relatives in Australia. If the Mages hadn't rescued you, your corpse would have been on the bottom of the Indian Ocean. <br /> <br /> Getting copies of lost books, or scanning them into a recorder is also a major job. <br /> <br /> The lost libraries of Yemen are a particular focus of New Parnassus (the city The Council of Twelve is headquartered in) just now. But Oxford, Cambridge, Baghdad, Constantinople, and Alexandria, all get attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T15:48:15-07:00","id":1493076,"title":"","content":"Calafia is the center of government, arts, and education on the planet Adocentyn. Calafia (which is the name of the black woman California was named after) is a large fertile island. If you placed a correctly sized outline of Calafia on map of North America, Calafia would extend from about seventy miles North of Vancouver to about two hundred sixty miles south of Tijuana. Calafia is a bit wider than California and the climate is very similar except somewhat wetter. <br /> <br /> New Parnassus is not the capital, it's a university town. If you still have the outline of Calafia over the West coast of North America, New Parnassus would be in about the same place as Monterey. The Capital is somewhat to the North and like San Francisco, it's around a great bay and natural harbor. <br /> <br /> More later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T14:13:48-07:00","id":1493131,"title":"","content":"To fit the genre and to allow Changelings to be the &quot;aliens&quot; in the crew we'll need Space Magic! (Yes I stole that from a show within a show from the Jetsons). <br /> <br /> Space Magic is basically two new arts. The Sight (sensory and clairsensory abilities) and Thought Crafting (telepathy and related abilities).<br /> <br /> So far I know the first level of The Sight is passive. Basically, you no longer botch sense rolls. Also, if you get any successes you add extra successes equal to the degree your glamour exceeds your banality, but not more than your level in this art. Yes this is powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T01:41:50-07:00","id":1493155,"title":"","content":"You might want to check out Mage: the Void. It was on Zanzibars sight before it shut down. It had a similar theme and could be mined for ideas. I'm pretty sure there is a backup still being hosted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T17:38:30-07:00","id":1506676,"title":"","content":"I decided that the twelfth sphere is Metamorphosis. Yes, I'm swiping that from another source. Metamorphosis is the sphere controlling all processes of change. And as everything is constantly changing this is a powerful sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T14:46:34-07:00","id":1506992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers?p=1492816#post1492816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the corporate or oligarchic state, problems could be delegated to groups of adventurers. The ensigns could be sent on a spy mission, undercover as an adventuring group from the region. First, they would have to observe locals and learn to speak and jest as they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Plutocratic Oligarchy (perhaps an outgrown of the Syndicate) would make an interesting foe. However I don't want the PCs to be the representatives of an Oligarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T02:11:51-07:00","id":1507168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers?p=1493131#post1493131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To fit the genre and to allow Changelings to be the &quot;aliens&quot; in the crew we'll need Space Magic! (Yes I stole that from a show within a show from the Jetsons).<br /> <br /> Space Magic is basically two new arts. The Sight (sensory and clairsensory abilities) and Thought Crafting (telepathy and related abilities).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some straightforward questions about Thought Crafting powers and abilities.<br /> <br /> Is it the case that they do include bolstering (and also altering, expanding, or enhancing) the thinking (and also emotions, ideas, attitudes, or ruminations) of the caster ? Do at least some of these powers and abilities allow the user to increase his own spirituals, psychic, and mental capabilities, processes and qualities ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-02-2023, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T05:24:07-07:00","id":1507175,"title":"","content":"A self awareness/self-editing level before the mind healing/thought redaction levels? That makes tons of sense.<br /> Level One: Would need to be Telepathic Communication.<br /> <br /> Level Two: Would need to be Mind Probing.<br /> <br /> Level Three: Telepathic Suggestion (These Droids aren't the ones your looking for) and illusion projection.<br /> <br /> Levels four and five would follow your suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-08-2023, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T16:35:11-07:00","id":1507794,"title":"","content":"I assume that paradox is possible in space. Away from Sleepers paradox is an aspect of the limitations of the Mage themselves. Internal barriers they need to deal with as part of their transformation and growth. <br /> <br /> I'll need to look up the differing limits on magic caused by population. Because of the pressure/influence of other living wills, magic is more difficult on higher population worlds. <br /> <br /> Also the cultures of a world can decide what is coincidental or vulgar in a given local. I'll draw on the Victorian Mage book for ideas about that. <br /> <br /> But it seems to me that, on a planet with only a population about the same as New Zealand's, paradox would work differently at the Void Engineers scout base than at the Hermetic college.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T18:03:58-07:00","id":1507809,"title":"","content":"My treatise on the nature of the Consensus (linked in my signature) suggests that the notion of Reality Zones comes in part from the notion of spatial separation; and that if significant equivalents of high-level Correspondence Effects have been integrated into the Consensus, it may be possible for Reality Zones to become homogenized. <br /> <br /> In particular, if the setting's technology includes \u201cmundane magic\u201d (that is, stuff that doesn't even register as sorcery anymore, let alone Sphere Magic) that's comparable to Co-Location (such as, say, something like Star Trek holodeck technology being used to allow you to interact physically with whomever is on the other end of a commlink), then sites linked together by this technology would arguably all be part of a single, shared Reality Zone. <br /> <br /> More generally, you might want to put some thought into how much \u201cmundane\u201d technology has advanced: there are things that we can do with mundane technology today that required Sphere Magick back in the 90s when Mage was first published; and I see no reason why that trend wouldn't continue into the future. So you might want to look at each of the Spheres and decide what Effects have mundane counterparts in your setting. Looking just at Correspondence, physical Co-Location technology is one fairly extreme example, possibly <i>too</i> extreme; but Star Trek style transporters or SG-1 style Stargates might be examples of some Correspondence \u2022\u2022\u2022 Effects that have entered the realm of \u201cmundane science\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T19:36:44-07:00","id":1507817,"title":"","content":"I would also suggest that if Conventional Space can be pushed out from lunar orbit to the Asteroid Belt in 20 years (1993 to 2013), then given a century or so it will <i>easily </i>extend out to cover <i>at least</i> the entire Solar System; at a minimum, the Spatial Horizon should be at the edge of the heliosphere (where the solar wind stalls out and the interstellar medium begins), and maybe even far enough to encompass other star systems. Perhaps at some point there's a breakthrough that ends up extending it out to the edge of the Milky Way Galaxy, making the Deep Umbra intergalactic space and everything within the galaxy either Conventional Space or Etherspace. <br /> <br /> Though I could see saying that each star is surrounded by its own bubble of Conventional Space that extends out to its equivalent of the Heliopause, and that the interstellar medium counts as Deep Umbra \u2014 not unlike the Spelljammer concept of wildspace inside a Crystal Sphere and Phlostigon outside of it, but without the Crystal Sphere. That would generally limit Correspondence Effects to within a single star system, with conjunctional Spirit/Dimension Science needed to create or work with an interstellar connection. It would also let you play with the notion that reach star system has its own version of Conventional Space, which may or may not be compatible with Earth's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T15:46:52-07:00","id":1510131,"title":"","content":"Having just gotten <b>Victorian Mage </b>on Thursday I see the Elegant/Uncanny/Catastrophic system as useful for this setting. Yes it's basically a tweak. But it's a really useful one. <br /> <br /> As the low populations on the new worlds would suggest lower difficulties in casting. I'm thinking something more like the scourge would fit this setting better than paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T18:46:23-07:00","id":1510141,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage Made Easy</b> suggests, among other things, that you might replace Paradox altogether, going with Resonance instead. Not so much \u201cReality bites back\u201d as \u201cactions have consequences\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T07:40:32-07:00","id":1510200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492812-starting-a-space-opera-game-looking-for-friendly-kibitzers?p=1510141#post1510141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mage Made Easy</b> suggests, among other things, that you might replace Paradox altogether, going with Resonance instead. Not so much \u201cReality bites back\u201d as \u201cactions have consequences\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's solid. Since, except for the Earth (a special case) everyone is aware of Magic and Mages. The average mage isn't overcoming reality's resistance, their facing their own internal issues. <br /> <br /> Earth is going to have been in a slow time envelope created by a deal between an Archmage and Wrinkle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T19:51:55-08:00","id":1547407,"title":"","content":"The Second Level of the Sight would be Telempathy. In others words awareness of the emotions and life energies of other beings.<br /> <br /> The third level of the sight would be psychometry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}